  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Onward Transport and Cash Assistance to Returnees Affected by Sudan Crisis.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The outbreak of fighting in Sudan on 15 April 2023 has severely affected the humanitarian situation in South Sudan, particularly in northern states of the country. Since the onset of the crisis, the influx of people fleeing Sudan has increased sharply at multiple border points between Sudan and South Sudan, in particular in Upper Nile, Northern and Western Bahr el Ghazal States. 
 
Through this project, IOM is providing life-saving interventions to the most vulnerable new arrivals in South Sudan who face protection, health and physical risks. IOM is providing Onward Transportation Assistance (OTA) to returnees who are travelling from Renk to Malakal and then to their final destinations which include Bentui, Juba, Kaujok, Fangak, Wau, Nasir and Fangak.</narrative>
  </description>
